//@ compile-fail
//@ requires: madaros
//@ error-pattern: E270
//@ description: #2354 / ADR-020 D-25 — `println(n as string)` on an integer is refused with E270, the same refusal the f64 print and the integer binding already get. Madaros only, and that is a measurement, not a preference: lean_single compiles this statement (2026-10-25, committed seed) and prints the integer, because its cast path leaves EXPR_TY alone for `integer as string` so println dispatches to emit_print_int. The ruling's "on both engines" is therefore not the current behaviour on lean_single; closing that half needs a refusal there, which is a lean_single change.

fn main() -> i64 with IO {
    let n: i64 = 42
    println(n as string)
    0
}
